-- 5. Quests whose story or objective line is different on live (not only a placeholder like $1oa or a line break).
-- 17 Uldaman Reagent Run
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='I''ve heard about a newly discovered plant called the magenta fungus caps.  They grow in clusters, deep in the Uldaman dig site; they may be elsewhere, but for now that''s the only place I know they''re at.  I want to study their potential use in alchemy, and that''s where you come in.\n\nFind the magenta cap clusters and bring me a dozen caps.  Be warned, the clusters may spew out poison spores if jostled.\n\nDo this for me, and I''ll whip up a batch of my famous greater mender''s potion for you!' WHERE `ID`=17;
-- 305 In Search of the Excavation Team
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='You cannot imagine how worried I have been.\n\nMy wife, Merrin, has been sending me letters each week for the past month. She is part of the Whelgar Excavation team. But it has been nearly two weeks since her last correspondence. Surely something is wrong!\n\nLongbraid said that he would send a scout to check up on things if we did not hear from the team soon. I assume that scout is you, $n. Find Merrin at the excavation site to the east!' WHERE `ID`=305;
-- 310 Bitter Rivals
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='I have to admit, those Thunderbrews make some good drinks. But they need to learn that theirs isn''t the only decent brew! Maybe you can help me teach them that lesson...\n\nHere, take this barrel of Barleybrew Scalder. Sneak into the basement of the Thunderbrew Distillery in Kharanos and switch it with one of their barrels of Thunder Ale. Then we''ll see how their patrons like my brew over theirs!\n\nAnd if the barrels are guarded, then you might have to distract the guard...' WHERE `ID`=310;
-- 429 Wild Hearts
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='My brother Quinn was badly hurt by the ghoul, Ivar the Foul, and I don''t know if he will heal properly without alchemical aid.  Although I am not an apothecary, I do know that our apothecaries can make healing potions from the discolored hearts of worgs.\n\nGather such hearts and take them to Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher to the south.  Then return here with the potion.\n\nYou can find plenty of worgs between here and Malden''s Orchard to the east.', `LogDescription`='Gather 3 discolored worg hearts and bring them to Apothecary Renferrel at the Sepulcher.' WHERE `ID`=429;
-- 465 Nek'rosh's Gambit
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='The Dragonmaw are closer to enacting their attack plans than we thought.\n\nNek''rosh has built catapults and aims to lay siege to Menethil! And with the fighting in Dun Algaz, we''re effectively blocked from reinforcements!\n\nYou need to take out those catapults. They''re in the Dragonmaw encampment.\n\nHere, take this tinder. Fight your way to the catapults and light them with the tinder.\n\nAnd after you''ve done that, find and kill Nek''rosh. We need to cut this Dragonmaw beast down...at its neck.' WHERE `ID`=465;
-- 515 Elixir of Agony
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='A mudsnout composite?  Absolutely brilliant!  Why didn''t I think of that?\n\nLet me contribute my colloid of decay to this devilish brew.\n\nIn order to activate the contaminating agents in this mudsnout mixture, Lydon is going to need a strong troll''s blood elixir, as well as some daggerspine scales and torn fin eyes from the southern coast of Hillsbrad.  He''ll know what to do once you''ve gathered him all the reagents.  And my, how anxious I am to hear how his experiment goes!', `LogDescription`='Bring the Mudsnout Mixture, a Strong Troll''s Blood Elixir, 5 Daggerspine Scales and 5 Torn Fin Eyes to Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill.' WHERE `ID`=515;
-- 544 Prison Break In
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Find the traitors and recover their artifacts, then return to me, $n.' WHERE `ID`=544;
-- 545 Dalaran Patrols
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Before it mysteriously vanished, there was an enormous magical barrier around the newly-reconstructed city of Dalaran. I care not what caused such a magical marvel to fail, but I do care that the newly exposed outskirts of their city may hide valuable magical treasures. Vestiges of the ruins on which the new city is built. \n\nBut the area is patrolled by the wizards and their elemental slaves.\n\nSo hunt them, and return when their numbers are sufficiently reduced.' WHERE `ID`=545;
-- 922 Rellian Greenspyre
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='$n, can you take one of the seeds you brought me to my friend, Rellian Greenspyre?  He is a druid in Darnassus, and when last we spoke he revealed his interest in my work with the Timberlings.  He had some ideas himself, and he will appreciate a specimen seed to work with.\n\nThank you, $n.  You have been a great help to me.  I hope that, some day, you will see the fruit of my labors.\n\nYou will usually find Rellian walking the pathways of the Cenarion Enclave in Darnassus.' WHERE `ID`=922;
-- 940 Teldrassil
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Deliver the Inscribed Bark to Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus.' WHERE `ID`=940;
-- 1045 Raene's Cleansing
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Kill 4 Bloodtooth Guards and retrieve Ran Bloodtooth''s Skull for Krolg near Lake Mystral.' WHERE `ID`=1045;
-- 1057 Reclaiming the Charred Vale
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Keeper Albagorm on Stonetalon Peak wants you to slay 6 Bloodfury Harpies, 6 Bloodfury Ambushers, 6 Bloodfury Slayers and 6 Bloodfury Roguefeathers.' WHERE `ID`=1057;
-- 1250 The Missing Diplomat
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='The Defias didn''t pay me well enough to die for their cause. They took the king. Yeah, the king of Stormwind, not some lowly diplomat. He was on his way to Theramore to meet with Jaina Proudmoore--it was a big deal apparently, and a big secret. But it''s not just the Defias that are involved. They''re working with someone. I think they knew this was bigger than them.\n\nMy part was just to get their man on board the king''s ship while it was moored. The guy''s name was Hendel. That''s all I know. I swear!' WHERE `ID`=1250;
-- 1267 The Missing Diplomat
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Speak to Jaina Proudmoore in Dustwallow Swamp.' WHERE `ID`=1267;
-- 1425 Deliver the First Shipment
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='While I fix this wagon, $n, I have one last task for you.\n\nI have packed the most vital supplies saved from the Lost Ones'' attacks. Take them to Nethergarde Keep. The keep is nestled in the northern hills of the Blasted Lands, keeping watch over the Dark Portal.\n\nTo reach Nethergard, follow the road east. When it branches head south into the Blasted Lands, then turn left at the next fork. Follow the road, $n, and be wary.' WHERE `ID`=1425;
-- 1472 Devourer of Souls
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='A sayaad is a devourer of souls, dominator of wills, tempter of hearts. A creature of profound evil and singular mind.\n\nFolk tales told by righteous and wicked alike use their common name: succubus for females, incubus for males.\n\nThe demon must be lured into our world with a stimulus - the hearts of pure and loving mortals. The sayaad will be unable to resist. Then you can dominate it, and make it your own.\n\nSpeak with my assistant, Godrick Farsan, within the temple. He will help you find your bait.' WHERE `ID`=1472;
-- 1476 Hearts of the Pure
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Coaxing a succubus will require the hearts of the pure. But is any mortal without vice?\n\nThrough bits of overheard stories, I found two humans that should do.\n\nThe first is Dalin Forgewright, who has dedicated himself to the care of the Lordaeron refuges, whom are refused by their kin at the Greymane Wall.\n\nThe other is Corma Villard, a woman who remains faithful to her lost love, wandering the Wetlands for a sign of her.\n\nDeliver their hearts to Carendin. But first, let me show you your quarry.', `LogDescription`='Bring the hearts of Dalin Forgewright and Corma Villard to Carendin Halgar in the Temple of the Damned.' WHERE `ID`=1476;
-- 1507 Devourer of Souls
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='The time has come for you to learn more of the summoning magics. You will learn to summon a sayaad, a creature of incredible mental powers. It can lull those of weak minds into its servitude--but have no fear! I feel certain that you will be equal to the challenge.\n\nA sayaad can only be summoned when baited with an item that represents great devotion and love. I leave it to you to find such an object.\n\nA suggestion? Speak with Cazul... There seems to be little the ancient warlock does not know.' WHERE `ID`=1507;
-- 1508 Blind Cazul
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='If Gan''rul has sent you to me, it must be that you are to summon a succubus, a female of the sayaad race, and need an object to use for enticement.\n\nHmm... If you trust a blind man to lead you, $n, then listen. In the bluffs of Orgrimmar, west of the wind rider tower, lives Zankaja. She waits for the return of her mate.\n\nGo to her.' WHERE `ID`=1508;
-- 2139 Tharnariun's Hope
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='The survival of our people and lands comes at unfortunate costs, $n.\n\nYou have spilled the blood of nature''s servants; many sick animals you have felled. The people of Auberdine are indebted to you, for the forest''s pain is eased--even if only for a moment.\n\nI have one final task for you, but be warned, you will have to kill again. It is my hope that this will be the last time I call upon you, $n.\n\nIn a cave to the northeast, near Bashal''Aran, resides the Den Mother. Slay her.' WHERE `ID`=2139;
-- 2202 Uldaman Reagent Run
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='I''ve heard about a newly discovered plant called the magenta fungus caps.  They grow in clusters, deep in the Uldaman dig site; they may be elsewhere, but for now that''s the only place I know they''re at.  I want to study their potential use in alchemy, and that''s where you come in.\n\nFind the magenta cap clusters and bring me a dozen caps.  Be warned, the clusters may spew out poison spores if jostled.\n\nDo this for me, and I''ll whip up a batch of my greater mender''s potion for you!' WHERE `ID`=2202;
-- 2203 Badlands Reagent Run II
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='You have been most helpful to me, $c.  I would reward you with the very recipe for the potion I gave you earlier... but I would ask of you a task that is quite dangerous.  Hear my request.\n\nThis lockbox contains three empty thaumaturgy vessels; they are imbued with an attunement aura that will drain the blood of a scorched guardian dragon.  Using one on the beast will anger it greatly, so be warned.  Once you have all three filled, bring them to me.\n\nDo this, and the recipe will be yours.' WHERE `ID`=2203;
-- 2501 Badlands Reagent Run II
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='You have been most helpful to me, $n.  I would like to reward you with the very recipe for the potion I gave you earlier, but I must ask of you a favor that is quite dangerous.\n\nThis lockbox contains three empty thaumaturgy vessels; they are imbued with an attunement aura that will drain the blood of a scorched guardian dragon.  Using one on the beast will anger it greatly, so be careful.  Once you have all three filled, bring them to me.\n\nDo this, and the recipe will be yours.' WHERE `ID`=2501;
-- 3441 Divine Retribution
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Listen as Velarok Windblade tells his story.' WHERE `ID`=3441;
-- 3442 The Flawless Flame
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Collect 4 Hearts of Flame and 4 globes of Golem Oil and return the items to Velarok Windblade.' WHERE `ID`=3442;
-- 3443 Forging the Shaft
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Bring 8 Thorium Plated Daggers to Velarok Windblade.' WHERE `ID`=3443;
-- 3452 The Flame's Casing
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Find and return a Symbol of Ragnaros to Velarok Windblade.' WHERE `ID`=3452;
-- 3453 The Torch of Retribution
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Wait for Velarok Windblade to complete the Torch of Retribution.' WHERE `ID`=3453;
-- 3518 Delivery to Magatha Grimtotem
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='The first tablet goes to a tauren ... one called Magatha Grimtotem. She is among the elders in Thunder Bluff, and is one of the proponents of the alliance between the tauren and the Forsaken. She, more than anyone among the elders, feels the tauren and their ways can help the Forsaken find a path back to being human.\n\nBring her the Tablet of Beth''Amara. The tablet may be the link she needs in finding a way to help the Forsaken... or so she claims.', `LogDescription`='Bring the Tablet of Beth''Amara to Magatha Grimtotem in Thunder Bluff.' WHERE `ID`=3518;
-- 3842 A Short Incubation
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='The Moonweavers, huh? Most intriguing. I wish the sprite darters could truly appreciate what it means to have those two look after them. They are both quite capable.\n\nSo, they gave you the egg as a gift. Well, then you should be responsible for it for as long as you desire. It appears it''s almost ready to hatch, but we should ensure it''s healthy.\n\nI only need two elixirs of lesser fortitude for a small spell to protect the egg. I have the rest of the components here with me.' WHERE `ID`=3842;
-- 4022 A Taste of Flame
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Show Cyrus Therepentous the Black Dragonflight Molt you received from Velarok Windblade.' WHERE `ID`=4022;
-- 4402 Galgar's Cactus Apple Surprise
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='It sure gets hot out here in the Valley of Trials.\n\n<Galgar wipes his brow.>\n\nIf only I had some cactus apples, I could make my famous cactus apple surprise! Nothing cools you off faster than a piece of that delicious treat.\n\nI''ll tell you what, $n. If you bring me 10 cactus apples, I''ll make you a few portions of cactus apple surprise to take with you on your adventures, and a free training manual, too. If you''re interested, you can find cactus apples growing near the cactus plants around here.' WHERE `ID`=4402;
-- 5047 Pip Quickwit, At Your Service!
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='You''ll find Malyfous Darkhammer in Everlook, $c. Tell him that ''Pip is A-OK'' and that the suit works perfectly.\n\nThen hand him this:\n\n<Pip hands you a glowing piece of flesh.>\n\nI snatched it from the beast''s innards during my ''vacation.''\n\nI bet Malyfous could give you a fairly accurate assessment of what he can do with parts from a monster like this!\n\nOh, I suppose you don''t know where Everlook is, do you? To Winterspring, $g fella:lady;!' WHERE `ID`=5047;
-- 5064 Grimtotem Spying
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Locate and retrieve the three Secret Notes in Darkcloud Pinnacle.' WHERE `ID`=5064;
-- 5214 The Great Ezra Grimm
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Terrible thing... what happened to Ezra. You see, the town was sacked and Ezra didn''t want to leave his precious goods behind. The last thing I remember him saying was, ''I''ll burn every last leaf before they get their damned, dirty hands on them!''\n\nI may love a good stogie but I''m no fool. I left Ezra and his delightful store that day. I assume he went down in flames but if there''s a chance that even one box of his famous tobacco is still intact...\n\nWhat do you say, $n? Find a box for ol'' Smokey?', `LogDescription`='Find Ezra Grimm''s smoke shop in Stratholme and recover a box of Grimm''s Premium Tobacco. Return to Smokey LaRue when the job is done.' WHERE `ID`=5214;
-- 5321 The Sleeper Has Awakened
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='I was on my way to Maestra''s Post to meet Liladris Moonriver, but I decided to stop here and take a short nap. Ever since I awoke from the emerald dream, I have been so sleepy...\n\n<yawn>\n\nAnd I can''t find my things anywhere! Would you mind helping me find them?\n\nI understand that Maestra''s Post is south of here, along the road in Ashenvale. I had come from that way...\n\nLastly, I may fall asleep so if you ever need to wake me, please use my horn. You''ll find it in the chest here.', `LogDescription`='Escort Kerlonian Evershade to Liladris Moonriver south along the road to find his bag in Darkshore.' WHERE `ID`=5321;
-- 5634 Desperate Prayer
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='A priest recently visited our halls seeking you out, young $r. He said that he was on a mission to find you and that you should return to the Hall of Mysteries in Ironforge as soon as possible. When you arrive, seek out High Priest Rohan--he will tell you more.\n\nThe Light be with you, $n.', `LogDescription`='Speak to High Priest Rohan in Ironforge.' WHERE `ID`=5634;
-- 5635 Desperate Prayer
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='You''ve caught the attention of our superiors, $n. They''ve asked you travel to the Hall of Mysteries in Ironforge as soon as possible. Apparently they feel you''ve proven yourself already and are prepared to further your training. When you get there, find High Priest Rohan. He will be able to guide you further. Good luck, and may the Light be with you.', `LogDescription`='Speak to High Priest Rohan in Ironforge.' WHERE `ID`=5635;
-- 5636 Desperate Prayer
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Elune bless you, good $r. I hope your Light finds you and protects you well this day.\n\nOne of your priests was here not long ago looking for you. He mentioned you returning to the Hall of Mysteries as soon as possible to speak with High Priest Rohan. It seems you''ve done well to garner such attention. I wouldn''t spend too much time here--your people have need of you.', `LogDescription`='Speak to High Priest Rohan in Ironforge.' WHERE `ID`=5636;
-- 5637 Desperate Prayer
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Time''s come for you to head to Stormwind, $n. High Priest Rohan in the Hall of Mysteries wants to speak to you. Gotta be somethin'' really good or really bad for the High Priest to want you there personally, but I''m guessin'' you''ve only done well for yourself and it''s a good thing that he wants to speak to ya.\n\nBut don''t waste too much time ''round here. I''d head there as soon as you can.', `LogDescription`='Speak to High Priest Rohan in Ironforge.' WHERE `ID`=5637;
-- 6134 Ghost-o-plasm Round Up
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='There''s a valley to the southeast, the Valley of Bones, haunted by centaur ghosts.  Sounds scary, doesn''t it?  Well think how scary it is to the centaur!\n\nHere, take this crate of ghost magnets.  If you place one between the two big skeletons in the valley, the Dead Goliaths, then ghosts will wander to it.  Distance yourself, take out the ghosts and get their ghost-o-plasm.\n\nI have a sneaking suspicion the Magram are VERY interested in this gunk. I plan to sell it to ''em.' WHERE `ID`=6134;
-- 6282 Harpies Threaten
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Tauren take pride as the protectors of these lands. Undoubtedly you can guess why I am alarmed with the number of harpies that dwell here in Stonetalon.\n\nThe Bloodfuries are the source of the increasing number of harpies in Kalimdor; they encroach upon all likes of life preventing the innocent from leaving their boundaries.\n\nI need you to cull the harpies, $n!' WHERE `ID`=6282;
-- 7481 Elven Legends
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Several years ago, a lone elven master named Telmius Dreamseeker fled the devastation of his homeland with several ancient elven artifacts in tow.\n\nOur search for this lost master lead us from the ruins of Quel''Thalas, through the Burning Steppes, across the great expanses of the sea, to Feralas.\n\nWe suspect that the elf sought sanctuary in the halls of Eldre''Thalas (what is now known as Dire Maul).\n\nYou must find him, adventurer. Whether alive or dead, the knowledge he carried must be recovered!', `LogDescription`='Search Dire Maul for Telmius Dreamseeker. Report back to Sage Korolusk at Camp Mojache with whatever information that you may find.' WHERE `ID`=7481;
-- 7482 Elven Legends
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Several years ago, a lone elven master named Telmius Dreamseeker fled the devastation of his homeland with several ancient elven artifacts in tow.\n\nOur search for this lost master lead us from the ruins of Quel''Thalas, through the Burning Steppes, across the great expanses of the sea, to Feralas.\n\nWe suspect that the elf sought sanctuary in the halls of Eldre''Thalas (what is now known as Dire Maul).\n\nYou must find him, adventurer. Whether alive or dead, the knowledge he carried must be recovered!', `LogDescription`='Search Dire Maul for Telmius Dreamseeker. Report back to Scholar Runethorn at Feathermoon with whatever information that you may find.' WHERE `ID`=7482;
-- 7724 Fiery Menace!
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Wouldn''t ye know it, every time ol'' Hansel wants to take a moment to relax and reflect upon his life, the powers that be give him another job.\n\nMe gots to think, come on! Ye know what I be saying? Come. On.\n\nSo, these here searing lava spiders are causin'' a ruckus o'' some sort. Oilfist says they shoot fire out their... erm, yea well, anyway, such things upset the children.\n\nI guess we gots to kill ''em. Rather, ye gots to kill ''em.' WHERE `ID`=7724;
-- 7788 Vanquish the Invaders!
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Beyond this tunnel you will find a field of strife and turmoil, young $c. The Horde continue to decimate our sacred forest, cutting down the evergreen foliage to power their machines of war.\n\nEnter Warsong Gulch and defend Silverwing Hold. Push back the invading Horde forces!\n\nDo this, and earn a talisman of merit.  Bring me such a talisman, $n, and I shall reward you.' WHERE `ID`=7788;
-- 7789 Quell the Silverwing Usurpers
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='The wilds of the Ashenvale forest will succumb to the might of the Horde, $r. Nothing the Silverwing say or do can stop our sovereign imperative. Kalimdor belongs to the Horde. How dare they attempt to prevent us from harvesting what is rightfully ours!\n\nLet the pride swell in your chest as you cut down their weak attempts at slowing our progress. Destroy the Silverwing Sentinels, and earn a Warsong mark of honor.  Return to me with such a mark, $n, and you will be rewarded.\n' WHERE `ID`=7789;
-- 7874 Quell the Silverwing Usurpers
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='The wilds of the Ashenvale forest will succumb to the might of the Horde, $r. Nothing the Silverwing say or do can stop our sovereign imperative. Kalimdor belongs to the Horde. How dare they attempt to prevent us from harvesting what is rightfully ours!\n\nLet the pride swell in your chest as you cut down their weak attempts at slowing our progress. Destroy the Silverwing Sentinels, and earn a Warsong mark of honor.  Return to me with such a mark, $n, and you will be rewarded.\n' WHERE `ID`=7874;
-- 8155 Arathi Basin Resources!
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='War must be fought with soldiers, any soldier will tell you.  They''ll also say that a battle fought with poor gear or on an empty stomach is lost before it starts!\n\nThat is why Arathi Basin is important.  There are key areas in the basin that hold essential resources.  Metals, weapons, food, lumber - all are needed, and all can be gained there.\n\nThat is what I want from you, $n.  Enter Arathi Basin, win the battle by holding more bases than the enemy, and return to me with a crate of resources.', `LogDescription`='Win the battle for Arathi Basin, get an Arathi Resource Crate, and return it to Sergeant Maclear at Refuge Pointe.' WHERE `ID`=8155;
-- 8161 Cut Arathor Supply Lines
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='The League of Arathor is sparing no expense in their move to retake Arathi.  They, and all the races of the Alliance, now stream to this distant region, intent on expanding their hold from Refuge Pointe.  We must stop them, and the best means to stop them is to take their supplies.\n\nYou can help us, $n.  Enter Arathi Basin, known for its rich mines, fertile land and skilled craftsman.  Capture and control every base you can, win the battle, and return to me with the resources you gain.', `LogDescription`='Win the battle for Arathi Basin, get an Arathi Resource Crate, and return it to Deathstalker Mortis at Hammerfall.' WHERE `ID`=8161;
-- 8162 Cut Arathor Supply Lines
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='The League of Arathor is sparing no expense in their move to retake Arathi.  They, and all the races of the Alliance, now stream to this distant region, intent on expanding their hold from Refuge Pointe.  We must stop them, and the best means to stop them is to take their supplies.\n\nYou can help us, $n.  Enter Arathi Basin, known for its rich mines, fertile land and skilled craftsman.  Capture and control every base you can, win the battle, and return to me with the resources you gain.', `LogDescription`='Win the battle for Arathi Basin, get an Arathi Resource Crate, and return it to Deathstalker Mortis at Hammerfall.' WHERE `ID`=8162;
-- 8425 Voodoo Feathers
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Your honor has brought some peace to me.  It is only right that I offer you something in return.\n\nMy weapons and armor were splendid in life, and yet they are of no use to me now.  They would be better served in your possession.\n\nTravel to the sunken temple and destroy the troll guardians Gasher, Mijan, Zolo, Hukku, Zul''lor, and Loro.  They carry magic feathers that can reform my physical body long enough to grant you rewards.' WHERE `ID`=8425;
-- 91282 A Second Home
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='It is encouraging to see my newly risen brothers and sisters thrive as you have. It is only through community and shared faith that we can truly realize our full potential however, and to that end we''ve begun to form a new paladin order right here in Tirisfal. \n\nIf you wish to learn more, you should visit our monastery on the edge of the Whispering Woods. It is called Bandarion Keep. It''s on the bluffs just northwest of the Solliden Farmstead, and should be hard to miss.' WHERE `ID`=91282;
-- 91733 Downstream
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='I was bringing back a supply shipment from the trading post, but my wagon tipped over and the supplies fell in the river! Before I could catch them, they had already washed downstream.\n\nBetween the murlocs and wolves down there, I don''t stand a chance of retrieving the supplies on my own. You seem like the hardy sort. Do you think you could find them for me?' WHERE `ID`=91733;
-- 91860 A Grim Fate
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Out on patrol last night I spotted a group of gnolls dumping a very large body onto a pyre on the shores of Fenris Isle. I didn''t see an elf or any smaller corpses, but I''d say this doesn''t bode well for them.\n\nIf you are brave or stupid you are welcome to charge into Fenris Isle to learn more, but if you ask me, it''s a lot of work to find some snooty elf that''s probably long dead.\n\nI know you paladins love swearing oaths and taking on lost causes, but this one isn''t worth it. Trust me.' WHERE `ID`=91860;
-- 91861 Into Fenris Keep
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='<The fact that you found only one body is a hopeful sign. Perhaps the High Elf that Trevan and Hadrec described is still alive somewhere deeper inside the nearby fortress?>' WHERE `ID`=91861;
-- 92109 My First Alchemy Set
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Bring 5 Empty Vials, 5 Silverleaf, and 5 Peacebloom to the young, aspiring alchemist inside the barn of Moonbrook in Westfall.' WHERE `ID`=92109;
-- 92432 An Alarming Request
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='I bring ill tidings from Dalaran. Something has disrupted our leylines, causing erratic and destructive behavior from our constructs in the city.\n\nWe know not yet what is causing this mayhem. The high council has ordered us to keep this matter private so as to not bring shame to our order. But we cannot keep up this charade forever. The city is being overrun as we speak!\n\nArchmage Modera has dispatched me to solicit outside aid. Seek her image out near Dalaran beside Lordamere Lake.' WHERE `ID`=92432;
-- 92458 Heart of Disruption
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Whatever disturbed the leylines, it started at the top of the Violet Citadel. A thunderous crash rang out from the parlors above, and now we are overrun with rampant arcane power. It''s taking all we have just to keep the wards in place.\n\nWe cannot afford to stall any longer. We need help.\n\nThe Kirin Tor are busy inside, but you will still need a less public approach to gain entry. Take this key and meet me in the citadel once you''ve made your way into the city. We must put an end to this disruption.' WHERE `ID`=92458;
-- 92467 Call of Earth
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='A sapta is a drink created to bind our spirits to the elements. Fused with magic, the potion will allow the strong willed to see the elements as no one else can. Your spirit will be connected to the element the sapta was created for, and only a select few shaman know the recipe.\n\nThe sapta is always drunk in a sacred place, and never anywhere else--remember that.\n\nSeek out the Rise of Spirits up the pass east of here. Drink your sapta there, and... well, you will see what you need to see.' WHERE `ID`=92467;
-- 92597 Reading the Leylines
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Here in the elemental plane, we derive much of our arcane strength from leylines that still run through the ground under our feet. Of late, these leylines have begun to pierce the surface, giving us more direct and powerful access to these latent arcane energies.\n\nGo to the standing stones to the northeast. There is a leyline there. Tap into your birthright and draw in its energy.', `LogDescription`='Use your Read Leyline racial ability at the leyline in Thendal Grove.' WHERE `ID`=92597;
-- 92750 Detonation at a Distance
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='I assume you want a "controlled" explosion? Not as much fun, but a good choice if you want to keep all your limbs.\nI''m afraid I don''t have a remote detonator--why don''t you go check with the sneaky folks down at Stormwind Intelligence? They should be able to find us something.' WHERE `ID`=92750;
-- 92751 Detonation at a Distance
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='You need something destroyed? Would this have anything to do with your activities in Moonbrook? Don''t look surprised. SI:7 stays apprised of all that goes on in Stormwind''s lands.\n\nIf you''re planning to set off an explosion in the caves below Westfall, you''ll want to be well outside beforehand. Take this remote detonator--it''s a recent prototype from our own engineers.\n\nOh--and it would be best if you didn''t mention my involvement to your elf friend.' WHERE `ID`=92751;
-- 92752 Explosive Consultation
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='That''s it--the bomb''s ready to go! Careful with that detonator, now.' WHERE `ID`=92752;
-- 94007 Taming the Beast
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Report to Quel''ana Quickgale in Valanaar.' WHERE `ID`=94007;
-- 94413 A Magical Affront
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='The recent emergence of the leylines on the surface of Zephras has been profound for our order. We have more direct and tangible access to the energies that permeate this place and it has increased our understanding of said magic greatly.\n\nThe Windshapers, however, view these emergences as scars on the land that must be "healed". This is an affront to our order and is something we simply cannot abide.\n\nGo to the leyline in the forest to the southwest and drive off the Windshapers you find there.' WHERE `ID`=94413;
-- 94440 A Lesson in Divinity
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Retrieve the Scarlet Crusade Attack Plans from the Scarlet Crusaders at Venomweb Vale, and return to Deathguard Billmuth at Bandarion Keep.' WHERE `ID`=94440;
-- 94441 A Lesson in Divinity
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Please give my thanks to Danitha Morr and tell her that the rest of the Deathguard will hear about the service that the paladins of Bandarion Keep performed for us. \n\nYou have a lot of promise as a paladin, and I am proud to have those like you among the ranks of the Forsaken. Dark Lady watch over you, $n.' WHERE `ID`=94441;
-- 94493 A Sacrifice in Vain
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Thank goodness our message got to Lotheluum. Wait, where are the rest of the reinforcements? Surely it is not just you they sent?\n\n<Elegael pales as you explain yourself.>\n\nSo the message did not get to Valanaar. We are in dire straits indeed then.\n\n<Elegael sighs deeply then looks resolute.>\n\nThen we must handle this on our own. Time is of the essence.' WHERE `ID`=94493;
-- 94822 Confounding Flash
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='You''ve caught the attention of our superiors, $n. They''ve asked you to travel to the Hall of Mysteries in Ironforge as soon as possible. Apparently they feel you''ve proven yourself already and are prepared to further your training. When you get there, find High Priestess Mims. She will be able to guide you further. Good luck, and may the Light be with you.' WHERE `ID`=94822;
-- 94824 Confounding Flash
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Time''s come for you to head to Ironforge, $n. High Priestess Mims in the Hall of Mysteries commands you to come speak with her. Gotta be somethin'' really good or really bad for the High Priestess to want you there personally, but I''m guessin'' you''ve only done well for yourself and it''s a good thing that she wants to speak to ya.\n\nBut don''t waste too much time ''round here. I''d head there as soon as you can.' WHERE `ID`=94824;
-- 94914 Moonglade
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Use the spell "Teleport: Moonglade" to travel to Moonglade. When you arrive, speak with Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven.' WHERE `ID`=94914;
-- 95111 An Underrated Talent
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='In Tarren Mill there is a weaponsmith known as Ott. By all accounts he is an unremarkable smith, selling simple blades to travelers. I purchased a sword from him myself, and when I took it to the undercity for maintenance some time later, the smiths there were surprised at its quality. They assumed it came from a well-known master smith, but no, it was just Ott.\n\nI''d like to give this orc a chance to do something truly special. Take the materials to Ott in Tarren Mill and offer him the commission.' WHERE `ID`=95111;
-- 95140 Old Fire-Eye
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Use the Moonsilver Blade to destroy Old Fire-Eye in Silverpine Forest.' WHERE `ID`=95140;
-- 95795 Fallen in the Fen
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Return to Dorin Songblade.' WHERE `ID`=95795;
-- 96044 Camping 101: Blacksmithing
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Speak with Tognus Flintfire in Kharanos to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.' WHERE `ID`=96044;
-- 96045 Camping 101: Alchemy
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Now that you''ve taken up Alchemy, I can also teach you how to craft a Mana Well for your camp once you''ve learned a bit. Build one of these and all of the healers and spellcaster types will come running to get a refreshing taste.' WHERE `ID`=96045;
-- 96058 Camping 101: Engineering
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Engineers like yourself can cook up all sorts of bits, bots, and bombs for fun and profit.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Reagent Bot for your camp. This helpful automaton can help keep you well-supplied so that you and your allies never run out of the materials needed to fuel your spells.' WHERE `ID`=96058;
-- 96059 Camping 101: Enchanting
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Now that you''ve begun your journey into being an enchanter, I reckon I can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp once you''ve learned the ropes.\n\nIt''s so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again.' WHERE `ID`=96059;
-- 96391 Underground Map
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='The map you are holding seems to show a complex series of underground tunnels and highways that all seem to converge on a point underneath Ironforge itself.\n\nYou can''t be sure what the runes say as they are written in the ugly jagged rune language of the Dark Iron dwarves, but you can guess at the purpose of these tunnels. As you are reading the map, a gust of wind washes over you and you can faintly hear a dwarven voice carried on it. Earthseer Farsen needs to see this.' WHERE `ID`=96391;
-- 96604 The Great Outdoors
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Lok-tar, $c. I can see you''ve got the look of an adventurer about you. This is good. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.\n\nYou''ll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful in this line of work. Not sure how your outdoor skills are but I can probably teach you a thing or two, if you''d be apt to learn.\n\nHave a seat near the fire and get comfortable. I''ll walk you through it.' WHERE `ID`=96604;
-- 96605 The Great Outdoors
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Sit near Kaga''s Basic Campfire and wait until you receive the Boosted Rest buff.' WHERE `ID`=96605;
-- 96898 Remnants of War
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='It wasn''t long ago that the citadel of Naxxramas bore down upon this city, intent on wiping the Forsaken off the map. Both the Forsaken and the Argent Dawn lost much that day to secure the future of the Forsaken.\n\nDuring the battle, the great necrotic focusing crystal mounted atop Naxxramas was shattered and its fragments were scattered all over this area. I suspect that is what the cultists are here for. Help me recover the fragments and deprive the Scourge of them.' WHERE `ID`=96898;
-- 97005 Chol'aruk the Ravener
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='There are rumors of a colossal abomination that makes its lair at a cave to the northwest of here, on the plateau known as Thorn Hill. The Razormane call it Chol''aruk or "The Ravener" and those that have seen it say it''s so massive that it can swallow an orc whole.\n\nFew believe such tales, but I do... because I''ve fought one like it myself. On the honor of those I lost to these things, this beast must die.\n\nGather strong allies and find the lair of Chol''aruk. Kill the abomination and bring me its head.' WHERE `ID`=97005;
-- 97220 Philmor's Favor
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Bring the Gatehouse Shipment to the stockroom entrance located in Trias'' Cheese shop in the Trade District.' WHERE `ID`=97220;
-- 97287 Shrewd Negotiations
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Speak with the Image of Archmage Modera near Dalaran.' WHERE `ID`=97287;
-- 97915 Camping 101: Alchemy
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Speak with Alchemist Mallory in Elwynn Forest near Stormwind to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.' WHERE `ID`=97915;
-- 97918 Camping 101: Engineering
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Engineers like yourself can cook up all sorts of bits, bots, and bombs for fun and profit.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Reagent Bot for your camp. This helpful automaton can help keep you well-supplied so that you and your allies never run out of the materials needed to fuel your spells.' WHERE `ID`=97918;
-- 97952 Camping 101: Blacksmithing
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Speak with Basil Frye in Undercity to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.' WHERE `ID`=97952;
-- 97954 Camping 101: Engineering
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Engineers like yourself can cook up all sorts of bits, bots, and bombs for fun and profit.\n\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Reagent Bot for your camp. This helpful automaton can help keep you well-supplied so that you and your allies never run out of the materials needed to fuel your spells.', `LogDescription`='Speak with Graham Van Talen in Undercity to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.' WHERE `ID`=97954;
-- 97958 Camping 101: Leatherworking
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Speak with Shelene Rhobart on the road to Undercity from Brill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.' WHERE `ID`=97958;
-- 97959 Camping 101: Mining
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Speak with Brom Killian in Undercity to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.' WHERE `ID`=97959;
-- 98025 WANTED: Jai'vhanel
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Attention!\n\nA reward is being offered for the death of the owl "Jai''vhanel" also known as "Swordfeather".\n\nUnfortunately this owl has gone mad and has begun to attack travelers as they journey along the road near Auberdine.\n\nJai''vhanel was last seen north of the Ameth''Aran ruins near the mountain base. Bring back one of her jet black feathers as proof of her death.\n\nReward claims for this bounty should be claimed with Sentinel Glynda Nal''Shea in Auberdine.\n\nThe Auberdine Village Council' WHERE `ID`=98025;
-- 98189 Return the Statuette
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Bring the Menethil Statuette to Captain Stoutfist in Menethil Keep.' WHERE `ID`=98189;
-- 98190 A Friend of the Family
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='You''ll want to take this to Stormwind right away. Proud as I am that this keep and harbor bears King Terenas Menethil II''s name, we are a calm harbor in a very nasty storm of enemies. It''s just not safe here.\n\nThe Dragonmaw in particular would sacrifice much to loot something like this... and I shudder to think of what they''d do with it.\n\nDon''t bother going up the chain of command on this one, $Glad:lass;. Go straight to Highlord Fordragon with this. He''ll know where it will be best kept.', `LogDescription`='Bring the Menethil Statuette to Highlord Bolvar Fordragon in Stormwind Keep.' WHERE `ID`=98190;
-- 98191 A Friend of the Family
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Bring the Menethil Statuette to Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker in the Cathedral of Light.' WHERE `ID`=98191;
-- 98326 Frosthowl
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Slay Frosthowl and collect the Sack of Fish for Gretta Ganter in Brewnall Village.' WHERE `ID`=98326;
-- 98392 Darkness in the Glade
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Collect Hatescreech''s Amulet, Windmistress Gaedress'' Amulet, and Witchmother Arysa''s Amulet for Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak in the Oracle Glade.' WHERE `ID`=98392;
-- 98394 The Great Cat Spirit
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Seek out the Great Cat Spirit in southern part Moonglade and learn what it has to share with you about the nature of the cat.' WHERE `ID`=98394;
-- 98396 The Great Cat Spirit
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Recover the Relic of the Fang, Relic of the Claw, and Relic of the Silent Shadow from the Stormrage Barrow Den, and return them to the Great Cat Spirit.' WHERE `ID`=98396;
-- 98423 The Treaty of Understanding
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='Inside of the vault you find a tablet detailing the terms of a peace treaty between the Bronzebeard and Wildhammer dwarf clans. It appears to date back to the time period just after the War of the Three Hammers, and is very likely a notable piece of dwarven history. The king of Ironforge would no doubt be interested in this artifact.' WHERE `ID`=98423;
-- 98731 Blessings of the Great Cat Spirit
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Speak to Dendrite.' WHERE `ID`=98731;
-- 98738 Blessings of the Great Windborne Cat Spirit
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Speak to Dendrite.' WHERE `ID`=98738;
-- 99046 The Lost Runner
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='The Council of the Forest sent a small group of sentinels to the Oracle Tree some time ago. The tree sends messages to our elders, and it falls to us to deliver them to Darnassus safely.\n\nI received word that our most recent runner has not yet arrived. The Oracle''s messages vary in frequency, but it has been abnormally long.\n\nPlease head towards the Oracle Glade along the road to the west and check on her. It would have been Eralya Leafshadow''s turn, and she is still in training. Elune guide you.' WHERE `ID`=99046;
-- 99047 Not Dead Yet
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Seek aid from Byancie in Dolanaar for Sentinel Eralya Leafshadow.' WHERE `ID`=99047;
-- 99049 Threat from Below
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `QuestDescription`='The nearby area is destroyed with obvious signs of a skirmish. Whatever ambushed Heglan didn''t make it out unscathed. There''s probably signs nearby of what happened.\n\nOrgnil will probably want to see any evidence left by the attackers.' WHERE `ID`=99049;
-- 99053 Escaping Ban'ethil
UPDATE `quest_template` SET `LogDescription`='Help Sentinel Lynessa Duskblossom escape Ban''ethil Barrow Den, and report her safety to Sentinel Kyra Starsong in Dolanaar.' WHERE `ID`=99053;

